{"data":{"cost_usd":0.0316,"model":"claude-opus-5-5","ok":true,"output":{"candidate_improvements":[{"evidence":"The Performance table and the 'Better than luck?' section are both empty. An empty section looks the same whether nothing happened or the reporting is broken.","how_to_test":"Generate next week's report and check that every portfolio from the pre-registration appears with a starting value, and that blank sections show an explicit status message. This needs no change to the portfolios themselves.","idea":"Make the report fill in every section even when there is no activity: list each portfolio with its starting value, 0 trades and 0 costs, and print 'not computed (n too small)' in the luck test."},{"evidence":"The ledger holds 7 entries while runs, trades and AI decisions are all 0. Their origin is unexplained.","how_to_test":"During shakedown, check that the reconciliation balances every week. Deliberately inject a test entry in a sandbox copy and confirm it gets flagged.","idea":"Add a reconciliation line comparing ledger entry count with expected entries (setup records + runs + trades + AI decisions), and flag any mismatch."}],"caveats":"There are no performance, cost or trading figures here at all, so no conclusions about strategy, skill or costs are possible. Even once data arrives, single weeks will be dominated by noise. The main goals of the remaining shakedown weeks should be to confirm that nightly runs actually happen, that trades and costs get recorded, and that AI spend stays within the cap. The improvements above concern reporting and process only, not trading rules, since there is no trading evidence yet to justify strategy changes.","strengths":["The ledger tamper check is already running and passed (7 entries verified), so record integrity is being checked from the start.","The API spending cap ($50 per month) is defined and reported, and spend is at $0.00, so cost exposure is controlled before any trading begins.","There is a clear separation between shakedown and scored periods (scoring begins 14 December 2026), which protects the pre-registered results from start-up glitches.","The report structure already tracks reliability items (missed runs, data errors, risk-manager actions), which is the right focus for a shakedown."],"summary":"This report covers Day 0 of the unscored shakedown, so there is essentially nothing to judge yet. No portfolio values, returns, trades or costs are shown, no AI calls were made ($0.00 of the $50 monthly stop spent), and no nightly runs were scheduled or completed (0 of 0). The only substantive check is that the ledger tamper check passed on 7 entries. That is a reasonable starting state, but it tells us nothing about whether the system works as designed, what it costs, or whether anything beats luck. Scoring does not start until 14 December 2026, which leaves about three weeks of shakedown to confirm the machinery runs end to end.","weaknesses":["The Performance table is completely empty. Not even the portfolio names or starting values are listed, so we cannot confirm the portfolios exist and are funded as intended.","The 'Better than luck?' section is blank with no explanation. It should explicitly say 'not computed: insufficient data' rather than appear broken.","Nightly runs show 0 of 0, so the scheduler has not yet been demonstrated working. 'None missed' is uninformative when none were due.","The ledger has 7 entries despite 0 runs, 0 trades and 0 AI decisions. That is probably setup records, but the report does not say what they are, so it cannot be cross-checked."]},"purpose":"weekly_review","searches":[],"sources":[],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":[{"cost_usd":0.0316,"in":1051,"out":1372}],"web_search_requests":null},"hash":"230c9d1d4a29e9877c414ec37eb8d47eba6591662002703e1b3bdbd431812349","prev_hash":"c2af46833cada45b13777c092dfe5107de1f1e84ee86e846de0b5ec6f979f98b","seq":8,"ts":"2026-11-23T20:22:21+00:00","type":"ai_call"}
